//
// PROBE: concat_with_space, its alias sp, drop_stacks and clear_stacks.
//
// The last four in-scope words a default build could bind and did not.
// F176 says why the two nesting words have nothing to show.

"probe: concat_with_space appends to the textbuffer beneath, a space between" println
"" convert.to_textbuffer "a" concat_with_space "b" concat_with_space println

"probe: sp is concat_with_space" println
"" convert.to_textbuffer "a" sp "b" sp println

"probe: the first piece brings no space" println
"" convert.to_textbuffer "only" sp len println println

"probe: an empty piece still brings its space" println
"t" convert.to_textbuffer "" sp len println println

"probe: the piece is converted to a string first" println
"" convert.to_textbuffer 42 sp 1.5 sp true sp :ptr sp nodata sp println
"" convert.to_textbuffer [ 1 2 ] sp println
"" convert.to_textbuffer dict sp println
"" convert.to_textbuffer '{"a":1}' json sp println

"probe: a textbuffer appended to a textbuffer stays one" println
"x" convert.to_textbuffer "y" convert.to_textbuffer sp type.of println println

"probe: drop_stacks inside a context changes nothing about how it closes" println
1 2 ( 5 drop_stacks ) take println current println

"probe: nor does clear_stacks, two contexts deep" println
( 5 ( 6 clear_stacks ) ) take println take println current println

"probe: after @name, drop_stacks leaves endcontext a context to close" println
@a 3 drop_stacks endcontext take println current println

"probe: with no context open both are silent" println
drop_stacks clear_stacks current println
